      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Polygon Energy installed my solar system which has been mostly working well since being installed. I opted to use high end Aiko panels and a Sungrow inverter. This came at an increased price.However, the install and quality was let down in a few areas:1. Using a cheap railing system to mount the panels which was unexpected given the premium price. It's still unclear to me if the mounting system even has the necessary engineering certifications.2. Over $1000 in unexpected additional electrical work cost after already attending on site, agreeing the price and scope. This is despite Polygon removing an upgrade cable between Main and Sub switchboards from scope.3. Poor quality electrical enclosure installation which damaged some of the brickwork and render at the front of my house, and requires post-install repairs which Polygon's subcontractors were unable to do.Given it was at the front of the house aesthetic aspects could have been dealt with better. I.e. using a high quality black railing system to match the all-black panels.I raised concerns regarding this and gave Polygon Energy and opportunity to rectify the electrical enclosure work which partially happened (albeit only fixing electrical components not the other damage). This is despite assurances from the Company Management it would be done with high quality and to Australian Standards.Polygon ultimately was the most expensive provider that I was quoted by, when factoring in additional costs, and thus I've rated them down to 2/5 for value for money. Overall 3/5.",
